   $q$Which revision of sentence 5 uses the most precise description to show what happened to the clay?$q$, $q$[{"text":"My clay, which was on the wheel, moved in a way.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-language"},{"text":"My clay was from the pottery studio on Saturday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-old-detail"},{"text":"My clay wobbled like jelly, then sagged and flopped onto its side.","is_correct":true},{"text":"My clay did something strange and did not work well.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-language"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$My clay wobbled like jelly, then sagged and flopped onto its side.$q$, $q$Exact verbs like "sagged" and "flopped" and the comparison to jelly help the reader picture the clay. The choice about the studio on Saturday repeats information from sentence 1 and does not describe the clay at all.$q$, 'draft', '17febbae-d75f-5efe-b245-0b2022ffa14c')
