   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence after sentence 7 that shows the narrator's feelings and keeps the same point of view. Which sentence does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"My cheeks burned, and I wondered if I would ever get it right.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The narrator felt embarrassed and wanted to give up on pottery.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"shifts-point-of-view"},{"text":"Pottery wheels have been used in many countries for a very long time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Mr. Okafor secretly thought I was the worst student he had ever had.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"narrator-knows-others-thoughts"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$My cheeks burned, and I wondered if I would ever get it right.$q$, $q$The story is told by "I," so the narrator should share their own feelings, as this choice does with burning cheeks and a worried thought. The choice using "the narrator" switches to an outside point of view, and a first person narrator cannot know Mr. Okafor's secret thoughts.$q$, 'draft', '17febbae-d75f-5efe-b245-0b2022ffa14c')
