   $q$The writer wants to add dialogue after sentence 12 to show how Mrs. Delgado feels. Which choice does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Do you two like orange cats?\" she asked.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dialogue-no-purpose"},{"text":"\"Pepper is still lost somewhere,\" she said sadly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-events"},{"text":"\"Thank you both so much,\" she said, her voice shaking. \"I was so worried.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"I bought apples at the store today,\" she said.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dialogue-off-focus"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Thank you both so much," she said, her voice shaking. "I was so worried."$q$, $q$Her thanks and her shaking voice show relief after a scary afternoon. The choice saying Pepper is still lost does show a feeling, but it contradicts sentence 11, where Pepper is safely found.$q$, 'draft', '9486b3b9-edfe-54a1-8296-3bc1ac50b348')
