   $q$The writer wants to add Grandpa's words after sentence 10. Which dialogue best fits the events and moves the story forward?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"It is almost time for lunch,\" Grandpa said.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dialogue-no-purpose"},{"text":"\"Quick, look straight up at the sun now!\" Grandpa said.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-earlier-detail"},{"text":"\"Look, the sun is completely covered!\" Grandpa said.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-events"},{"text":"\"This is the biggest the bite will get,\" Grandpa whispered. \"Soon it will shrink.\"","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"This is the biggest the bite will get," Grandpa whispered. "Soon it will shrink."$q$, $q$Grandpa's words fit the crescent moment and prepare the reader for sentence 13, when the bite shrinks away. The choice telling the narrator to look at the sun is tempting because it sounds exciting, but it goes against Grandpa's warning in sentence 4.$q$, 'draft', '7f47078a-3e1b-5a9a-b377-48ed0abd9c51')
