   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 13 as a conclusion that follows from the events?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Later that year, Nana Ifeoma taught me how to bake bread.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"starts-new-event"},{"text":"My bike tire went flat the day before our class bike ride.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-situation"},{"text":"The next morning, I pedaled beside my class, proud that I now knew how to fix a flat myself.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Most bike tires have a rubber tube inside them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The next morning, I pedaled beside my class, proud that I now knew how to fix a flat myself.$q$, $q$This ending shows the narrator joining the ride and reflects on what they learned from Nana, so it wraps up the story. The sentence about the flat tire only repeats sentence 1.$q$, 'draft', 'f2771f24-c553-56c6-bd6d-90fdacbd670c')
