   $q$Why does the writer use the words "The most important reason" in sentence (3)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"to signal that the opinion piece is about to end","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"conclusion-signal-confusion"},{"text":"to state the writer's opinion for the very first time","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-reason-with-opinion"},{"text":"to show that the reasons are ordered and that safety matters most","is_correct":true},{"text":"to introduce a view that disagrees with the writer","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$to show that the reasons are ordered and that safety matters most$q$, $q$The phrase tells readers that safety is the writer's strongest reason, which organizes the reasons in a logical order. The opinion was already stated in sentence (2), so sentence (3) is not introducing it.$q$, 'draft', 'a22aad92-4772-59c1-b995-c886842375ae')
