        '3-5', $q$Turn Down the Lights$q$, $q$(1) On a clear night in our town, you can see only a few stars. (2) Our town should turn off the bright lights at the sports fields and parking lots after ten o'clock at night. (3) First, darker skies would let people enjoy the stars again. (4) Last summer, my family visited a campground far from any city. (5) We saw thousands of stars stretched across the sky like a glittering river.

(6) ______ fewer lights would help wildlife. (7) Many birds fly at night and use the stars to find their way. (8) Bright lights can confuse them and pull them off course. (9) Baby sea turtles have a similar problem near beaches that are lit up at night.

(10) Some people think dark parking lots would be unsafe. (11) The town could keep a few dim lights on near sidewalks and doors. (12) Turning lights off after ten would also save the town money on its electric bill.$q$, 'draft')
