        '3-5', $q$Wheelchair Basketball$q$, $q$(1) Wheelchair basketball is a fast and exciting sport. (2) Players move their chairs with their hands and dribble the ball at the same time. (3) The rules are mostly the same as in regular basketball. (4) ____, the hoop is the same height, and a basket still counts for two or three points. (5) There are a few differences, though. (6) ____, a player must pass, shoot, or dribble after pushing the wheels twice. (7) Players also use special chairs with slanted wheels that make sharp turns easier.

(8) Last spring, a wheelchair basketball team visited our school. (9) The players let us try their chairs during gym class. (10) I learned that turning and dribbling at the same time takes a lot of practice. (11) Our gym floor had been waxed the week before. (12) Most of all, the visit showed me how much skill and strength the sport takes.$q$, 'draft')
