   $q$Read the sentence: "The firefighters who were brave carried the ladder to the roof." Which revision says the same thing in fewer words?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The brave firefighters who were brave carried the ladder to the roof.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"still-repetitive"},{"text":"The firefighters carried the ladder to the roof.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-meaning"},{"text":"The brave firefighters carried the ladder to the roof.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The firefighters, who were brave, they carried the ladder to the roof.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"extra-subject"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The brave firefighters carried the ladder to the roof.$q$, $q$"Who were brave" can shrink to the single word "brave" in front of "firefighters." "The firefighters carried the ladder to the roof." is shorter, but it drops the detail that they were brave.$q$, 'draft', null)
