   $q$Read the sentences: "The storm came. The wind blew. The lights went out." Which revision makes these short, choppy sentences flow better without changing the meaning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"When the storm came, the wind blew and the lights went out.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The storm came and the wind blew and the lights went out.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"stringy-and"},{"text":"The lights went out, so the storm came and the wind blew.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"The storm came, the wind blew, the lights went out.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-unfixed"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$When the storm came, the wind blew and the lights went out.$q$, $q$Starting with "When" ties the events together in time and makes one smooth sentence. "The storm came and the wind blew and the lights went out." is joined, but a chain of "and" sounds just as choppy.$q$, 'draft', null)
