   $q$Read the sentence: "Zainab finished the swim race in a way that was very fast." Which revision is the most precise and least wordy?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Zainab finished the swim race in a fast way.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"still-wordy"},{"text":"Zainab finished the swim race swiftly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Zainab finished the swim race slowly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-meaning"},{"text":"Zainab finished the swim race and won a medal.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-new-facts"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Zainab finished the swim race swiftly.$q$, $q$The single word "swiftly" replaces "in a way that was very fast." "In a fast way" is shorter but still uses a wordy phrase where one adverb would do.$q$, 'draft', null)
