   $q$Tomas is writing a science report about wind turbines. Which sentence uses the formal language a report needs?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Wind turbines are, like, totally awesome at making power.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-informal"},{"text":"So basically the wind spins these turbine thingies.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-informal-slang"},{"text":"Wind turbines change the energy of moving air into electricity.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Wind turbines are fun to look at and pretty cool.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-fact"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Wind turbines change the energy of moving air into electricity.$q$, $q$This sentence uses exact, serious words that fit a report. The sentence "Wind turbines are, like, totally awesome at making power." has the same idea, but "like" and "totally awesome" are casual words for talking with friends.$q$, 'draft', null)
