  ('9b4dabec-d4c3-57f0-975d-e47017129f9d', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g5-precise-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Ingrid is writing a quick note to her classmate Dev about practicing their lines for the school play. Which sentence best fits a friendly note?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Lines after school or not, let me know whatever.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unclear-message"},{"text":"Rehearsal of dialogue shall occur after the final bell.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-formal-stiff"},{"text":"Want to practice our lines for the play after school?","is_correct":true},{"text":"I formally request your presence at a rehearsal of our lines.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-formal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Want to practice our lines for the play after school?$q$, $q$A friendly note to a classmate can sound relaxed, like everyday talk. "I formally request your presence at a rehearsal of our lines." is correct English, but it sounds stiff and strange between friends.$q$, 'draft', null)
