   $q$A student's museum report says: "The dinosaur skeleton in the main hall was cool." Which word would replace "cool" to make the report more formal and precise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"small","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-meaning"},{"text":"awesome","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-informal"},{"text":"nice","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-adjective"},{"text":"impressive","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$impressive$q$, $q$"Impressive" keeps the positive meaning of "cool" in a formal, exact way. "Awesome" is just as casual as "cool," so it does not fit a report.$q$, 'draft', null)
