   $q$Read the sentences: "Kenji checked the school weather station. He wrote the temperature in his notebook." Which choice best combines the sentences?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Kenji checked the school weather station, he wrote the temperature in his notebook.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-unfixed"},{"text":"Kenji wrote the temperature in his notebook before checking the school weather station.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-order"},{"text":"Checking the weather station, the notebook recorded the temperature.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-modifier"},{"text":"After checking the school weather station, Kenji wrote the temperature in his notebook.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$After checking the school weather station, Kenji wrote the temperature in his notebook.$q$, $q$"After checking" keeps the events in order and makes Kenji the one who did both. "Checking the weather station, the notebook recorded the temperature." makes it sound as if the notebook checked the station.$q$, 'draft', null)
