   $q$Read the sentences: "We went to the planetarium. We saw a show about Saturn. We learned that Saturn's rings are made of ice and rock." Which revision best varies the sentence beginnings without changing the facts?$q$, $q$[{"text":"At the planetarium, we saw a show about Saturn and learned that its rings are made of ice and rock.","is_correct":true},{"text":"We went to the planetarium, we saw a show, we learned about Saturn's rings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-unfixed"},{"text":"At the planetarium, we saw a show about Jupiter and learned that its rings are made of ice and rock.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-facts"},{"text":"We went to the planetarium and we saw a show and we learned that Saturn's rings are ice and rock.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"stringy-and"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$At the planetarium, we saw a show about Saturn and learned that its rings are made of ice and rock.$q$, $q$Opening with "At the planetarium" breaks the pattern of "We..." and joins the ideas smoothly. The choice about a show on Jupiter is built the same way, but it swaps Saturn for Jupiter.$q$, 'draft', null)
