        '3-5', $q$Draft: Bricks from Bottles$q$, $q$(1) The article "Bottles Into Bricks" by Amara Osei describes a small factory that turns used plastic into building bricks. (2) ____. (3) Osei explains that workers wash and shred plastic bottles and old containers. (4) Then they melt the pieces with sand and press the mix into molds. (5) She writes that the finished bricks are lighter than clay bricks but just as strong.

(6) The bricks also help keep plastic out of nature. (7) Osei reports that the factory uses about two tons of plastic each week that would otherwise go to a landfill. (8) ____, neighbors now bring their plastic trash to the factory instead of throwing it away. (9) This shows that the project changed how people in the town think about waste.

(10) Osei does point out one problem. (11) The melting machines use a lot of electricity. (12) Even so, the article shows that plastic bricks can solve two problems at once.$q$, 'draft')
