        '3-5', $q$Draft: What a Weather Journal Shows$q$, $q$(1) In "Keeping a Weather Journal," Priya Raman explains how writing down the weather each day can help people notice patterns. (2) Raman shows that a weather journal turns everyday observations into useful information. (3) She suggests writing down the temperature, the type of clouds, and the wind at the same time every day. (4) ____, she explains, the notes are easy to compare from one day to the next.

(5) Raman describes a fifth-grade class that kept a journal for one whole spring. (6) By May, the students noticed that tall, puffy clouds in the morning often came before an afternoon storm. (7) They began to bring umbrellas on those days. (8) This shows that their notes helped them predict the weather on their own.

(9) Raman also says a journal can show changes over a longer time. (10) One family compared their notes from two springs. (11) They found that the first warm day came about a week earlier the second year. (12) ____.$q$, 'draft')
