  ('5dcbb143-957a-5bfa-b278-545981dc6936', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-argument-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Why does the writer include sentences (6) and (7)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"to admit a fair opposing concern before answering it with a reason and evidence","is_correct":true},{"text":"to begin a new topic about how the school plans its daily schedule","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"to prove that every teacher at the school dislikes pen pal programs","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"to show that the writer has changed sides and now opposes the program","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mistakes-counterclaim-for-position"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$to admit a fair opposing concern before answering it with a reason and evidence$q$, $q$Sentences (6) and (7) acknowledge the worry about lost class time, and sentences (8) and (9) then answer it. The writer never changes sides, because sentence (8) begins with "However" and argues back.$q$, 'draft', '4a1d66de-fe3c-5482-9c57-7e168e6035b5')
