values
  ('eaabb5ed-de41-54b4-8f92-b762d9ba8775', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-argument-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Sentence (10) is too informal for an argument. Which sentence is the best replacement?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The town should also paint the benches on Main Street a brighter color.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"Still, tree roots might crack the sidewalks, so maybe the town should wait.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-claim"},{"text":"Honestly, trees are really nice to look at, and everybody should just like them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-informal-tone"},{"text":"For these reasons, the town council should approve a plan to plant trees on Main Street this year.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$For these reasons, the town council should approve a plan to plant trees on Main Street this year.$q$, $q$The correct sentence uses a formal tone and calls for the action the essay argues for. The choice about waiting gives in to the opposing claim the writer already answered in sentences (7) and (8).$q$, 'draft', 'ee5a62a6-c7ea-5541-82be-b8ea441a37dc')
