  ('83b6440f-6e5e-5df9-8b2b-ee1696271c30', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-argument-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which detail would best support the reasoning in sentence (5)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The writer enjoys walking to the library on cool autumn days.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weak-anecdote"},{"text":"Main Street has a bakery, a shoe store, and a small bookshop.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"lists-without-support"},{"text":"Oak trees can live for more than two hundred years in the right conditions.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"After a nearby town planted trees downtown, its store owners reported more customers on summer afternoons.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$After a nearby town planted trees downtown, its store owners reported more customers on summer afternoons.$q$, $q$Sentence (5) claims that cooler sidewalks would help businesses, and the nearby town's results show that happening. Listing the shops on Main Street names businesses but gives no proof that shade would help them.$q$, 'draft', 'ee5a62a6-c7ea-5541-82be-b8ea441a37dc')
