  ('c604a725-6da3-5e1c-88a6-5d6d05bc3c23', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-argument-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence after sentence (8) that explains how the response answers the business owners. Which sentence is best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Some roots may still break through the pavement after many years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weakens-claim"},{"text":"Planters can be made from wood, stone, or recycled plastic.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-detail-not-reasoning"},{"text":"This proves that tree roots have never damaged a sidewalk anywhere.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"With careful planning, the town can enjoy cooler streets without damaging the sidewalks shoppers use.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$With careful planning, the town can enjoy cooler streets without damaging the sidewalks shoppers use.$q$, $q$The correct sentence connects the solutions in sentences (7) and (8) back to the worry about cracked sidewalks. The choice saying roots have never damaged a sidewalk claims far more than the writer's evidence can show.$q$, 'draft', 'ee5a62a6-c7ea-5541-82be-b8ea441a37dc')
