   $q$How does sentence (5) help the writer's argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It gives a number that measures how fast students can type.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mislabels-reasoning-as-data"},{"text":"It repeats the main claim in the same words as sentence (2).","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"It explains why speed matters by connecting faster typing to more focus on ideas.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It admits that the opposing side has a reasonable point.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mislabels-reason-as-counterclaim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It explains why speed matters by connecting faster typing to more focus on ideas.$q$, $q$Sentence (5) is reasoning: it tells readers why typing speed is worth caring about, because students can think about ideas instead of keys. The numbers about words per minute appear in sentence (4), not sentence (5).$q$, 'draft', '78d35ea2-2fd1-59e5-b55b-d8ee6d5708f8')
