        '6-8', $q$The Sport of Curling$q$, $q$(1) Curling is a winter sport played on a long, flat sheet of ice. (2) Two teams of four players take turns sliding heavy granite stones toward a target. (3) The target is a set of painted circles called the house. (4) A team scores a point for each stone that ends up closer to the center of the house than any of the other team's stones.

(5) The most unusual part of curling is the sweeping. (6) After a player releases a stone, two teammates rush ahead of it with special brooms. (7) Sweeping warms the ice slightly, which creates a very thin layer of water. (8) This helps the stone slide farther and travel straighter.

(9) Curling takes skill and teamwork. (10) The player throwing the stone must aim carefully and push it with the right speed. (11) Meanwhile, the team captain, called the skip, stands at the far end and points to where the stone should go. (12) The sweepers listen to the skip, who calls out when to sweep harder or stop.$q$, 'draft')
