   $q$Which revision of sentence 6 uses the most precise description to show how the kite fell?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The kite went up and then it came back down onto the ground.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-language"},{"text":"The kite jerked upward, twirled like a falling leaf, and smacked into the grass.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The kite did something bad and did not work very well.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-language-telling"},{"text":"The kite, which was made of paper and sticks, fell to the ground.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"repeats-old-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The kite jerked upward, twirled like a falling leaf, and smacked into the grass.$q$, $q$Precise verbs like "jerked," "twirled," and "smacked," plus the comparison to a falling leaf, help the reader picture the crash. The choice about paper and sticks repeats information from sentence 2 instead of describing the fall.$q$, 'draft', '6618eca0-7c60-52a2-8e0c-92d1080a7c4a')
