   $q$The writer wants to replace sentence 11 with dialogue that moves the plot forward. Which choice does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mateo grinned. \"My hoodie string is long,\" he said. \"Let's add it.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Hello, my name is Mateo,\" he said to the woman.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dialogue-no-purpose"},{"text":"\"We will never fly this kite,\" Mateo groaned, so we packed up and left.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-later-events"},{"text":"\"I really like your red box kite,\" Mateo told the woman.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dialogue-off-focus"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Mateo grinned. "My hoodie string is long," he said. "Let's add it."$q$, $q$Mateo's idea to add his hoodie string leads straight into sentence 12, where the cousins fix the tail. The choice where they pack up is tempting because it has strong feeling, but it contradicts the rest of the story.$q$, 'draft', '6618eca0-7c60-52a2-8e0c-92d1080a7c4a')
