-- Passage wg6-narrative-writing-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('5dcb6018-76a4-5064-a032-3f562dd2fd3b', 'wg6-narrative-writing-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-narrative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Schoolhouse Bell$q$, $q$(1) Our class took a field trip to the Pinecrest Historical Society, which is inside a one-room schoolhouse built in 1890. (2) A volunteer named Mrs. Haddad met us at the door. (3) She showed us the wooden desks, the slates students once wrote on, and an iron stove in the corner. (4) Then she pointed to a thick rope hanging from the ceiling. (5) "Long ago, a student rang this bell every morning," she said. "Would anyone like to try?" (6) Every hand shot up, including mine. (7) She picked me. (8) I grabbed the rope and pulled as hard as I could. (9) Nothing happened. (10) My classmates giggled, and my cheeks turned warm.

(11) Mrs. Haddad smiled. (12) "It's not about pulling hard," she said. "It's about rhythm." (13) She showed me how to pull, let the rope rise, and pull again. (14) I tried it her way. (15) The rope swung up, and a deep DONG rolled across the room. (16) Some museums have gift shops near the exit. (17) Everyone clapped.

(18) That was the end of the field trip.$q$, 'draft')
