   $q$Which revision of sentence 9 best builds suspense by slowing the pace at this moment?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The rope stretched, the bell above me creaked once, and then the room went silent.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Nothing happened because old bells are heavy and made of metal.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"explains-instead-of-shows"},{"text":"Nothing happened, and the rest of the field trip went on as planned.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"skips-ahead"},{"text":"Nothing happened, so I let go and went back to my seat.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"rushes-past-conflict"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The rope stretched, the bell above me creaked once, and then the room went silent.$q$, $q$The correct choice stretches the moment with small details of the rope, the creak, and the silence, which makes the reader wait. The choice about heavy bells gives an explanation instead of showing the moment, and it does not match the real reason given in sentence 12.$q$, 'draft', '5dcb6018-76a4-5064-a032-3f562dd2fd3b')
