-- Passage wg6-narrative-writing-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('ab31b049-04b4-566d-8d22-6b253f7db2d3', 'wg6-narrative-writing-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-narrative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Anchor Leg$q$, $q$(1) The last event of the swim meet was the relay, and I was swimming the final leg. (2) Our team, the Riverside Otters, was tied with the Hillcrest Herons for first place. (3) As I stood behind the starting block, my knees felt like jelly. (4) Then our first swimmer, Grace, dove in. (5) The whistle blew. (6) She pulled ahead by half a body length. (7) Our second and third swimmers kept the lead, but the Herons were catching up. (8) Pools are usually kept at about the same temperature all year. (9) When our third swimmer touched the wall, I launched myself off the block.

(10) The water roared in my ears. (11) I kicked harder than I ever had in practice. (12) At the turn, I could see the Herons' swimmer right next to me. (13) I stretched my arm as far as it would go and slapped the wall.

(14) I looked up at the scoreboard. (15) We won.$q$, 'draft')
