   $q$The narrator's feelings change during the story. Which pair of sentences best shows this change?$q$, $q$[{"text":"sentences 5 and 9","is_correct":true},{"text":"sentences 4 and 11","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-events-with-feeling"},{"text":"sentences 3 and 12","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-setting-with-feeling"},{"text":"sentences 1 and 2","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-situation-with-feeling"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$sentences 5 and 9$q$, $q$Sentence 5 shows the narrator expecting boredom, and sentence 9 shows eager excitement as they write as fast as they can. Sentences 4 and 11 are tempting, but they show a change in the number of birds, not in the narrator's feelings.$q$, 'draft', '5925898f-3222-59bc-91fc-a09c9149d0af')
